# Digital-twin campaign.
#
# design/ IS committed - it is the single source of truth for Saltelli pairing,
# and run_ensemble.py refuses to start against a design whose SHA-256 does not
# match its sidecar.
#
# results/*.jsonl ARE committed on purpose: each machine writes its OWN file
# (..._machine0.jsonl ... _machine3.jsonl), so they can never merge-conflict,
# and committing them makes git the transport for tallying across machines
# while carrying the git/solver/workbook hashes along with the data.
#
# report/ is derived from results/ and is regenerated by merge_and_sobol.py.
digital_twin/report/

# NOTE: this file needs `git add -f` on first commit. The user's global ignore
# (~/.gitignore_global) starts with `.*`, which matches every dotfile including
# .gitignore itself - so without -f these rules would exist only locally and
# would not reach the other campaign machines.
